## Required Directories

{{layout_dirs}}

These directories are the current fixed layout contract. Treat `.agent/` and `scripts/agent_*.py` as governance surfaces, application directories as product code surfaces, and generated output directories as downstream artifacts unless this project records a different boundary here.

## Dependency Direction

- Governance policy and harness scripts may inspect application code, docs, specs, and manifests.
- Application code should not depend on mutable `.agent/` session, memory, runlog, or scoring state for runtime behavior.
- Generated artifacts should be downstream of source files and manifests; update source first, then regenerate or synchronize.
- Update this document and `.agent/dev-map.json` when module ownership or dependency direction changes.

## Decisions

- Use `docs/PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md` and `.agent/blueprint.json` as the global current architecture and runtime/framework contract after requirements interview.
- Link feature-level architecture changes to embedded spec changes through `.agent-spec.json#/blueprint_impact`.
- Link durable architecture decisions to embedded spec changes, `.agent/sessions/` decisions, or ADRs under `docs/adr/`.

